 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "my washin mashine wont turn on at all no lights nothin"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "If your washing machine is completely dead with no lights at all, the most common cause is simply that it isn't receiving electricity. This could be an issue with the wall socket, the plug, the lead itself, or a fused spur switch on the wall. Before we look inside the appliance, please confirm if the socket actually has power by testing it with another device like a lamp."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "the other sockets in the kitchen work, my kettle works fine. the washin mashine is built in behind a cupboard door so i cant reach the plug tho"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the socket works but the machine is dead and the plug is hidden, we need to check the connection path before assuming an internal fault. Many built-in machines are plugged into a switched socket or a fused spur unit behind the cupboard; if that switch is off or the fuse has blown, the machine will be completely dead. Please check if there is a wall switch controlling it and ensure it's on, and if you can see the plug end, verify the 13A fuse inside is intact."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i looked and theres a row of switches above the worktop, one says washer and its OFF. my flatmate must of switched it off when cleaning. i cant see the plug tho"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That explains it perfectly—since the switch was off, the machine wasn't receiving any electricity at all. Please turn that 'washer' switch back on and see if the machine powers up immediately."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i switched it back on and it lights up now and works!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That's excellent news. It was simply the switched spur being turned off, which is a very common cause for built-in machines to go completely dead. To avoid this happening again when you clean, just remember to check that switch before starting your laundry. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
